## Implementation Details

The Analytics component is correctly placed in the component tree:
```
<PaletteProvider>
  <PipelineRunProvider>
    <BrowserRouter>
      <Routes>...</Routes>
    </BrowserRouter>
  </PipelineRunProvider>
  <Analytics />  ← Correctly positioned at application root level
</PaletteProvider>
```

This placement ensures:
- Analytics tracks all routes in the application
- The component is outside the router but inside the providers
- Follows React best practices for third-party analytics integrations

## Documentation Reference
Implementation verified against official Vercel Analytics Quickstart Guide:
- URL: https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
- Framework: React/Vite
- Method: Component-based integration

## Next Steps for Deployment

To enable Web Analytics in production:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel: `vercel deploy`
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard (Analytics section)
3. Verify tracking by checking browser Network tab for `/_vercel/insights/*` requests

